<title>USA: Integ adopts shareholder rights plan.</title>
<headline>Integ adopts shareholder rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Integ Inc said Wednesday its board of directors adopted a shareholder rights plan aimed at thwarting takeover threats.</p>
<p>The company declared a dividend of one right for each common share outstanding on December 6. Integ said the rights will go into effect if a person or group accumulates 15 percent or more of its stock.</p>
<p>Integ did not specifically say whether the move is a response to a known threat. The company could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>Integ stock closed up 1/4 at 12-1/8.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
